From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: since30 stock 24-bit 0x45 + SPI CONTINUE

since29 put tcm_u16=4080 on each 0x45/CONTINUE packet. IC treated that
as the command length, IDENTIFYd after 4k, mode 0x02, and we stopped
because RomBoot was gone (remaining=93214).

u16=4080 is the SPI chunk size, not the TCM command length. Stock
write_message sets buf[1/2] = length (image+14 = 97294) which wraps
to 31758. reserved[0] = size>>16 (=0x01) makes a 24-bit length:
(0x01<<16)|31758 = 97294.

Chunking belongs inside one write_message(0x45, full_buf, image+14)
via HDL_WR_CHUNK_SIZE / CMD_CONTINUE_WRITE: first frame keeps stock
header, later SPI pages are CONTINUE with no new u16. Clock all
97294 bytes. IDENTIFY/0x1b after a SPI page is not firmware-started
unless remaining==0.

Keep: first drain, no lcd_rst, no IRQ printk flood, no ENABLE_REPORT
0x05, no do_polling, no IRQ unwind.

Applies after syna-tcm-romboot-per-chunk-u16.patch.

